==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|incident|al|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɪnsɪˈdɛntəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Loosely associated; existing as a [[byproduct]], [[tangent]], or [[accident]].
#: ''That character, though colorful, is '''incidental''' to the overall plot.''
# Entering or approaching, prior to [[reflection]] (more frequently [[incident]]).

====Related terms====
* [[incident]]
* [[incidence]]

====Derived terms====
* [[incidental expense]]
* [[incidentally]]
* [[incidental music]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} [[accidental]], [[contingent]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} [[inevitable]], [[necessary]], [[impossible]]

